  <section id="what-is-est" class="content-section reveal" aria-label="What is EST">
    <h2>2. What is EST (Eastern Standard Time)?</h2>
    <p>
      Eastern Standard Time (EST) is the standard time observed in the Eastern Time Zone of North America during the winter months. It operates at an offset of **UTC-5** (five hours behind Coordinated Universal Time). When it is 12:00 PM UTC, it is 7:00 AM EST on the East Coast.
    </p>
    <p>
      EST is observed in seventeen U.S. states in their entirety, parts of six other states, and several provinces of eastern Canada. The winter standard begins on the first Sunday in November and continues until the second Sunday in March.
    </p>
    <p>
      Major cities that follow Eastern Standard Time during winter include New York, Toronto, Montreal, Washington D.C., Boston, Atlanta, and Miami. In addition to North America, some Caribbean nations, such as Jamaica and Panama, observe EST year-round without daylight saving adjustments.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
