    <h2>6. When Does EST Change to EDT? (DST Schedule)</h2>
    <p>
      The transition between Eastern Standard Time and Eastern Daylight Time occurs twice a year on a standardized calendar schedule:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Spring Forward (EST to EDT)</strong>: On the second Sunday of March, at 2:00 AM local time, clocks are moved forward by one hour to 3:00 AM. This transition marks the beginning of EDT.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fall Back (EDT to EST)</strong>: On the first Sunday of November, at 2:00 AM local time, clocks are moved back by one hour to 1:00 AM. This transition marks the end of EDT and the return to EST.
      </li>
    </ul>

