    <p>
      To clarify timezone terminology, let us compare the three terms:
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table aria-label="EST vs EDT vs ET comparison table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Term</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Offset</th>
            <th>Typical Usage</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Eastern Time (ET)</strong></td>
            <td>General Zone Name</td>
            <td>Variable (UTC-5 or UTC-4)</td>
            <td>Best for year-round calendars and event invites.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Eastern Standard Time (EST)</strong></td>
            <td>Winter Offset</td>
            <td>Fixed (UTC-5)</td>
            <td>Used specifically from November to March.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Eastern Daylight Time (EDT)</strong></td>
            <td>Summer Offset</td>
            <td>Fixed (UTC-4)</td>
            <td>Used specifically from March to November.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- Custom Inline SVG for Year DST timeline (Image 7 replacement) -->
